{#- Atlas — surface one: feature planning (the accordion, #780's successor).

  Not a drawing. Each feature is a collapsed row; opening one reveals its milestone spine
  (theme/_includes/depth.njk's own expand block, wired by theme/order.js). No dates, no duration —
  the design doc for this rebuild is explicit that the milestone is the axis here, not a calendar.

  Data this layout expects — `workstreams`, in the order the config declares, each:
    slug, manifest { codename, stage, next, ownerAction, milestones: [{ id, label, depth, title, status, tasks }] }
    displayedStage — src/build.mjs's assembleSite: the manifest's own `stage`, overridden by a
                     deployment log's latest entry when the workstream has one (M8 task 6). The
                     chip renders THIS, never `manifest.stage` directly.
    deploymentHistory — src/build.mjs's assembleSite (M8 task 6): the ordered `{ stage, note }`
                     array read from `stream.manifest.deploymentLog`, or `[]` when the workstream
                     names no log yet. Rendered as `.stage-history` below, directly above (not
                     inside) `.milestone-spine` — a stage transition is a fact about the feature,
                     not about any one milestone (M8 design doc, "Where the ordered history
                     renders").
    column   — computeLadder's own entry: covered[], completedCount, milestoneCount, tipLabel
    triage   — src/triage.mjs's classifyTriage result
    milestones — url/planUrl/recordUrl-enriched, `.manifest` mirrors `manifest.milestones[i]`
    spineDetail — one 'full'|'full-muted'|'count'|'none' per milestone, same order

  M8 task 7's trigger buttons (Development/Staging/Release, `theme/deploy.js`) render only when
  `stream.manifest.deploymentLog` is set — the one build-time signal already on every workstream
  that says `POST /api/deployment-transition` has somewhere to write for it; without one, the
  endpoint itself refuses with `no-deployment-log` before writing anything
  (`api/lib/handlers.mjs`'s `handleDeploymentTransition`). No existing "write-back configured"
  template conditional was found to mirror (grepped `theme/`, `src/`, `api/` first) — `api/answer`
  and `api/acceptance` are real endpoints with no caller anywhere in `theme/`, so this is Atlas's
  first write-back UI, not a copy of one.

  `data-sha` (M8 task 7 fix round) carries `stream.deploymentLogSha` — the deployment log's own
  git blob SHA, computed at build time from the file's actual bytes on disk (`src/build.mjs`'s
  `gitBlobSha`), `""` when there is no log yet. `theme/deploy.js` reads this attribute directly
  instead of fetching a SHA from GitHub client-side at click time: every real Atlas project lives
  in a private repository (decision 7), so an unauthenticated client-side GET to GitHub's contents
  API always 404s there — the build-time value is the one that actually works.

  `data-log`/`data-repo` on the same wrapper are left over from the old two-step GET-then-POST
  design and are no longer read by `theme/deploy.js` (the server derives the log path from the
  manifest itself). Kept deliberately rather than stripped: they are still true, harmless metadata
  about which log and repo a row's buttons belong to, and a future caller (a debugging script, a
  future write-back UI) may want them without re-deriving from the manifest. Remove them if that
  stops being worth the two attributes.

  M9's proposed-design list (decision 59) moved to its own page, `backlog.njk` — "Feature Backlog"
  — at the owner's request; see that template's own header for the data shape and everything else
  that used to live in this comment.

  M9 follow-up: every milestone's full task checklist is now ALWAYS in the markup, not just the one
  `spineDetail` marks 'full'/'full-muted' — `spineDetail` still decides which milestones START
  expanded (an owner hit a real case, two milestones both `next` at once, where only the first one
  spineDetail picks got a checklist at all; the fix is client-side expand/collapse, not a smarter
  build-time pick). `theme/milestone-toggle.js` wires `[data-milestone-toggle]` the same way
  `theme/order.js`'s `toggleExpand` already wires `[data-row-handle]` — same `aria-expanded`/
  `aria-controls`/`hidden` mechanism, one level deeper. The page-level "Expand all"/"Collapse all"
  pair (`[data-milestones-expand-all]`/`[data-milestones-collapse-all]`) only ever touches milestone
  toggles, never a workstream's own `[data-row-handle]` — collapsing every feature row at once was
  not what was asked for, and the two controls already do different things.

  Decision 62 (draft): a task line may carry a real id now (`src/tasks.mjs`'s `parseTasks`,
  `T3 · Move dialog to…`). `data-task-id` on `.task-line` below is that id, present only when the
  issue actually wrote one — inert data, not a feature. No interaction reads it yet; it exists so
  a later, separately-decided approve/deny/defer/comment mechanism has something stable to address
  a task by, instead of the position-only `data-task-index` every task has always carried.
-#}
{% extends "base.njk" %}
{% import "base.njk" as ui %}

{% block bodyClass %}page page-planning{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<h1>Feature planning</h1>
<p class="lede">Expand a feature to see what it's doing right now.</p>

<div class="planning-controls">
<p class="controls-note">Drag a feature to reorder it, or press <kbd>H</kbd> to hide one — hidden features come back from the controls below.</p>
<div class="hidden-bar" data-hidden-bar hidden></div>
<p class="order-said" data-order-said role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
<div class="milestone-toggle-all">
<button type="button" class="milestone-toggle-all-button" data-milestones-expand-all>Expand all milestones</button>
<button type="button" class="milestone-toggle-all-button" data-milestones-collapse-all>Collapse all milestones</button>
</div>
</div>

<ul class="feature-list" data-feature-list>
{%- for stream in workstreams %}
<li class="feature-row" data-slug="{{ stream.slug }}">
<div
  class="feature-row-head"
  data-row-handle
  tabindex="0"
  role="button"
  aria-expanded="false"
  aria-controls="spine-{{ stream.slug }}"
  data-name="{{ stream.manifest.codename }}"
  aria-describedby="row-note"
>
<span class="disclosure" aria-hidden="true">▸</span>
<span class="feature-name">{{ stream.manifest.codename }}</span>
{{ ui.chip('stage', stream.displayedStage) }}
{%- if stream.column.milestoneCount %}
<span class="milestone-strip" role="img" aria-label="{{ stream.column.completedCount }} of {{ stream.column.milestoneCount }} milestones complete">
{%- for filled in stream.column.covered %}<span class="strip-seg{% if filled %} is-filled{% endif %}"></span>{% endfor -%}
</span>
{%- else %}
<span class="milestone-strip-empty">No milestones yet</span>
{%- endif %}
{%- if stream.column.tipLabel %}
<span class="feature-next">Next: {{ stream.column.tipLabel }}</span>
{%- elif stream.manifest.next %}
<span class="feature-next">{{ stream.manifest.next }}</span>
{%- endif %}
{{ ui.chip('triage', stream.triage) }}
{#- Decision 63 (draft): the chip above already says "Waiting on you" once `ownerAction` exists
    (src/triage.mjs) — this is the plain sentence saying what, right beside it, so a reader never
    has to open the row or parse `next`'s narrative prose to find out. -#}
{%- if stream.manifest.ownerAction %}
<span class="owner-action-text">{{ stream.manifest.ownerAction }}</span>
{%- endif %}
</div>
<a class="feature-link" href="{{ stream.url }}">View {{ stream.manifest.codename }}'s own page</a>
<div class="feature-spine" id="spine-{{ stream.slug }}" data-feature-spine hidden>
{#- Directly above .milestone-spine, not inside it (see the header comment above, and the M8
    design doc's "Where the ordered history renders"). Never blank: a workstream with no logged
    transitions yet still shows one node for its own current displayedStage, which is the
    pre-deployment case, not an empty state. -#}
<ol class="stage-history" aria-label="Deployment history">
{%- if stream.deploymentHistory.length == 0 %}
<li class="stage-node"><span class="stage-node-label">{{ ui.chipLabel(stream.displayedStage) }}</span></li>
{%- else %}
{%- for transition in stream.deploymentHistory %}
<li class="stage-node">
<span class="stage-node-label">{{ ui.chipLabel(transition.stage) }}</span>
{%- if transition.note %}<span class="stage-node-note">{{ transition.note }}</span>{% endif %}
</li>
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
</ol>
{%- if stream.milestones.length == 0 %}
<p class="spine-empty">No milestones on record yet.</p>
{%- else %}
<ol class="milestone-spine">
{%- for milestone in stream.milestones %}
{%- set detail = stream.spineDetail[loop.index0] %}
{%- set milestoneDetailId = 'milestone-detail-' + stream.slug + '-' + milestone.manifest.id %}
{%- set startsOpen = detail == 'full' or detail == 'full-muted' %}
<li class="milestone-node tone-{{ milestone.manifest.status }}" data-milestone-node="{{ stream.slug }}-{{ milestone.manifest.id }}">
<span class="milestone-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<div class="milestone-body">
<div class="milestone-head">
<a class="milestone-name-link" href="{{ milestone.url }}">
<span class="milestone-label">{{ milestone.manifest.label }}</span>
<span class="milestone-title">{{ milestone.manifest.title }}</span>
</a>
{%- if detail != 'none' and milestone.manifest.tasks.length %}
<button
  type="button"
  class="milestone-toggle"
  data-milestone-toggle
  aria-expanded="{{ 'true' if startsOpen else 'false' }}"
  aria-controls="{{ milestoneDetailId }}"
>
<span class="disclosure" aria-hidden="true">▸</span>
<span class="milestone-task-count">{{ milestone.manifest.tasks.length }} sub-task{{ 's' if milestone.manifest.tasks.length != 1 else '' }}</span>
</button>
{%- endif %}
{{ ui.chip('status', milestone.manifest.status) }}
</div>
{%- if detail != 'none' and (milestone.manifest.assignees.length or milestone.manifest.tasks.length) %}
<div id="{{ milestoneDetailId }}"{% if not startsOpen %} hidden{% endif %}>
{%- if milestone.manifest.assignees.length %}
<ul class="milestone-assignees{% if detail == 'full-muted' %} is-muted{% endif %}" aria-label="Assigned">
{%- for a in milestone.manifest.assignees %}
<li class="assignee">
{%- if a.avatarUrl -%}
<img class="assignee-avatar" src="{{ a.avatarUrl }}" alt="" width="16" height="16">
{%- endif -%}
{%- if a.htmlUrl -%}
<a class="assignee-name" href="{{ a.htmlUrl }}">{{ a.login }}</a>
{%- else -%}
<span class="assignee-name">{{ a.login }}</span>
{%- endif -%}
</li>
{%- endfor %}
</ul>
{%- endif %}
{%- if milestone.manifest.tasks.length %}
<ul class="task-list{% if detail == 'full-muted' %} is-muted{% endif %}" data-task-list data-milestone="{{ stream.slug }}-{{ milestone.manifest.id }}">
{%- for t in milestone.manifest.tasks %}
<li class="task-line{% if t.done %} is-done{% endif %}" data-task data-task-index="{{ loop.index0 }}"{% if t.id %} data-task-id="{{ t.id }}"{% endif %} aria-describedby="task-note">
<span class="task-check" aria-hidden="true">{% if t.done %}✓{% else %}○{% endif %}</span>
<span class="task-text">{{ t.text }}</span>
<span class="task-owner">{{ t.owner or 'Unassigned' }}</span>
</li>
{%- endfor %}
</ul>
{%- endif %}
</div>
{%- endif %}
</div>
</li>
{%- endfor %}
</ol>
{%- endif %}
{%- if stream.manifest.deploymentLog %}
<div class="stage-trigger" data-stage-trigger data-log="{{ stream.manifest.deploymentLog }}" data-repo="{{ repo }}" data-sha="{{ stream.deploymentLogSha }}">
<p class="stage-trigger-label">Record a deployment transition</p>
<button type="button" class="stage-trigger-button" data-transition-to="development" data-slug="{{ stream.slug }}">Development</button>
<button type="button" class="stage-trigger-button" data-transition-to="staging" data-slug="{{ stream.slug }}">Staging</button>
<button type="button" class="stage-trigger-button" data-transition-to="release" data-slug="{{ stream.slug }}">Release</button>
<p class="stage-trigger-status" data-stage-trigger-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
</div>
{%- endif %}
</div>
</li>
{%- endfor %}
</ul>

<p class="visually-hidden" id="row-note">Drag a feature's header to put the features in the order you want, or focus one and press the up and down arrow keys to move it. Press Enter or Space to open it. Press H to hide a feature; hidden features can be brought back from the controls above the list.</p>
<p class="visually-hidden" id="task-note">Drag a task to put this milestone's tasks in the order you want, or focus one and press the up and down arrow keys to move it.</p>
{% endblock %}

{% block bodyScripts %}
<script type="module" src="/order.js"></script>
<script type="module" src="/deploy.js"></script>
<script type="module" src="/milestone-toggle.js"></script>
{% endblock %}
